  "narrative": {
    "intro": "DDB Chicago had $303M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. DDB Chicago received 11 awards so far in the fiscal year, with an average award size of $27.6M. Obligations are down 22.4% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows fluctuating obligations: FY21 was $348M, FY22 was $363M, FY23 was $596M, FY24 was $399M, FY25 was $391M, and FY26 is $303M. The current-year totals are partial and reflect contract obligations rather than full award values for the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables. The award count and average award size indicate a program of relatively large awards rather than many small contracts. Recent fiscal history shows a peak in FY23 followed by declines in FY24, FY25, and FY26, with FY26 at $303M. This snapshot can help procurement and capture teams prioritize outreach and understand that current-year performance is a partial view of ongoing contract activity.",
